3	// Command-line regression tests for `edgefleet heartbeat health`.
4	//
5	// The domain rules (new-missed arithmetic, rollback detection, baseline
6	// validation) already have focused tests in package edgefleet. These tests
7	// protect what a user actually sees at the real command entry point:
8	//
9	//   - whether --missed-since-seq takes effect at all,
10	//   - the exact terminal output (cumulative missed stays on the first line,
11	//     baseline fields on the second),
12	//   - stdout vs stderr placement (health findings vs usage errors),
13	//   - and the process exit status (a health finding is not a command failure;
14	//     a bad baseline is).
15	//
16	// The tests re-execute the compiled test binary, which calls main() itself
17	// (see TestMain), so the code under test is the genuine command path — flag
18	// parsing included. Everything runs offline against a temp data directory
19	// with fixed receive/query instants, so no wall-clock waiting or network is
20	// involved.
